<div class="container">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <div class="last-updated">
        <strong>Last Updated:</strong> January 18, 2026
    </div>

    <p>At <strong>Lemon Slice Labs</strong>, we believe that privacy is a fundamental human right. Our philosophy is
        simple: we do not want your data. This policy outlines our commitment to privacy across our websites.</p>

    <h2>1. Our Core Principles</h2>
    <div class="principles-list">
        <p>Our lab operates on four unbreakable principles:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>No Personal Collection:</strong> We do not collect any personal information at all.</li>
            <li><strong>No Cookies:</strong> We do not use cookies on our websites, unless functionally required.</li>
            <li><strong>No External Tracking:</strong> We do not use external analytics, trackers, or third-party
                marketing tools.
            </li>
            <li><strong>No IP Storage:</strong> We never store your IP address anywhere.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>2. Website and Analytics</h2>
    <p>To improve our services, we aggregate strictly non-identifiable browser information via tools hosted on GitHub Pages:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>We track origin countries, device types, and screen sizes in aggregate.</li>
        <li>We use fully anonymized hashes as same-session identifiers. These cannot be traced back to an individual
            user.
        </li>
        <li>We host all our sites and tools through GitHub Pages, without the use of external subprocessors.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. GDPR and International Rights</h2>
    <p>For users in the European Economic Area (EEA), we comply with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
        Since we do not collect personal data, many of the standard "data processing" clauses do not apply. However, you
        maintain the right to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Inquire about any data we might hold (the answer will be "none").</li>
        <li>Complain to a supervisory authority if you believe our local-only processing violates your rights.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="contact-info">
